One recommendation before Phase-08

I think we should deliberately avoid calling the next phase "UI Components."

Instead, I recommend keeping the name Component Ecosystem, but redefining what a component means.

For COREI, a component should never be merely a reusable visual control.

Instead, every component should be classified as an Institutional Capability Component with a clearly defined operational responsibility.

For example, instead of organizing by technical type:

Button
Card
Table
Chart

we should organize by institutional purpose:

Observation Components — KPI strips, gauges, timelines, health indicators.
Analysis Components — relationship graphs, comparison matrices, dependency trees.
Execution Components — order tickets, approval panels, command consoles, action bars.
Monitoring Components — event streams, alerts, logs, telemetry views.
Knowledge Components — notebooks, documentation viewers, research panels.
Navigation Components — command palette, workspace switcher, breadcrumbs, object explorer.
Collaboration Components — comments, assignments, shared sessions, operator presence.

This continues the architectural principle we've established throughout Stage-23:

Institutional responsibility defines architecture.

Technical implementation follows architecture.

I believe that philosophy will make the COREI Component Ecosystem fundamentally different from a traditional component library and will provide a much stronger foundation for the remaining phases of the Institutional Operator Workstation.






